23:34:52.230   channel 0: port 8485, host decided per connection
23:34:52.230   channel 1: port 8486, host decided per connection
23:34:52.230 NOT AUTHENTICATED: a migration seed is a u32, so it identifies a pending
23:34:52.230   migration rather than proving who is on the far end. It is single-use.
23:34:52.230 THIS CHANNEL ANSWERS PACKETS - the default since 2026-09-14. It used to need
23:34:52.230   --set-field-probe, a flag every caller passed and whose absence cost a launch;
23:34:52.230   --silent-channel is the way to turn answering off now, and it is only for
23:34:52.230   eliminating the channel as a variable.
23:34:52.230   This channel answers: the migration hello with a SetField
23:34:52.231   carrying the character's real record (presence[0] the stat block, presence[2]
23:34:52.231   the equipped list), 0x00DC with that field's NPCs and mobs, 0x00D1 with the
23:34:52.231   portal's destination, 0x00E7 with the !map GM command, and 0x0151 with a
23:34:52.231   script Say, 0x0104 with the NPC shop, and 0x00D2 with a channel migration.
23:34:52.231   CONFIRMED on a real client: the dressed character, the bag and its 125 slots,
23:34:52.231   NPC dialogue, mobs spawning and moving, an unequip that survives a map change.
23:34:52.231   NOT yet seen on screen: the shop counter, the quest journal, the channel
23:34:52.231   switch. Dropping an item is refused on purpose - there is nowhere to put it.
